pycares: keep the ARES_OPT_LOOKUPS string alive until ares_init_options().

Channel.__init__ assigns a temporary straight to a struct field:

    options.lookups = _ffi.new('char[]', ascii_bytes(lookups))

cffi does not keep an owning cdata alive through a pointer stored in a struct
field, so the buffer is freed as soon as the statement ends, before
ares_init_options() copies it. c-ares can then read garbage lookup flags, and
Channel(lookups="f").getaddrinfo("localhost") fails intermittently. This
recipe's own build check hit it in most runs on linux-x86_64 (against c-ares
1.34.4 and 1.34.8). The fix holds a local reference until init, the way the
domains option already does.

Pending upstream: still present in pycares 5.1.0. Drop this patch once a
pycares release carries the fix.

--- a/src/pycares/__init__.py
+++ b/src/pycares/__init__.py
@@ -552,7 +552,10 @@
             options.evsys = _lib.ARES_EVSYS_DEFAULT

         if lookups:
-            options.lookups = _ffi.new('char[]', ascii_bytes(lookups))
+            # Keep the buffer alive until ares_init_options() has copied it: a
+            # temporary assigned to a struct field is freed straight away.
+            lookups_buf = _ffi.new('char[]', ascii_bytes(lookups))
+            options.lookups = lookups_buf
             optmask = optmask |  _lib.ARES_OPT_LOOKUPS

         if domains:
